 "text": "Hey, how are you doing these days? The seat tube usually has a sticker covering one its heights. Compare it to gears you' still happy with, and if you' short stop walking. Then try sitting a hole deeper, or a bit shorter if it' too deep already. You can move the seat tube a bit. Which part? Try sitting on it with a minimal amount of pad. Then you probably need shorter stem so you don't end up perching on the edge. Shorter stem yes, it'll make you turn slower. A shorter reach handlebar that twists slightly at the base is really bad.",
